      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Studies often suggest that East Asian leadership, rooted in collectivism, might favor indirect communication and building consensus to resolve team conflicts during a crisis. This approach prioritizes group cohesion over immediate assertion of self. In contrast, some research indicates that middle eastern leadership styles, valuing strong relational dynamics and directness, might lean toward more authoritative or direct conflict engagement to quickly establish order. Therefore, the typical pattern seen is a difference between harmony-seeking consultation versus direct assertive intervention.",
